{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you","id":544507,"title":"[Beast] Do Heroes seem a bit...anaemic to you?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-07T17:18:07-07:00","id":544507,"title":"[Beast] Do Heroes seem a bit...anaemic to you?","content":"I have to say, comparing the rules for Beasts to those for Heroes suggests that Beasts will <i>annihilate</i> Heroes unless the Hero is <i>much</i> more experienced than the Beast, or you have a team of Heroes ganging up on a Beast.<br /> <br /> Heroes are... rather underwhelming - am I the only one who gets this impression?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:45:59-07:00","id":544572,"title":"","content":"I think it's supposed to be a David vs. Goliath sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:55:34-07:00","id":544577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you#post544507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, comparing the rules for Beasts to those for Heroes suggests that Beasts will <i>annihilate</i> Heroes unless the Hero is <i>much</i> more experienced than the Beast, or you have a team of Heroes ganging up on a Beast.<br /> <br /> Heroes are... rather underwhelming - am I the only one who gets this impression?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of personal opinions about heroes and the way they, the intent of the writers was that they are arrogant and self centered assholes with delusions of grandeur.<br /> <br /> The base hero template being significantly weaker than the base Beast template plays into this.<br /> <br /> Think about it, what are the chances that a hero has the skills needed to kill a Beast? Really? going straight from civilian to Hero? Unlikely.<br /> <br /> So the heroes who make it past their first beast were either already badass Mofos, or they got really fucking lucky.<br /> <br /> Both of which feed back into those delusions of grandeur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:12:44-07:00","id":544602,"title":"","content":"Rater202, it <i>is</i> okay for people not to be as into the Hero vs Beast as-written-by-the-devs dynamic as you are, and you don't to jump into every protest about them feet first demanding that people see Heroes your way.<br /> <br /> As far as OP -- I think Heroes honestly could have been written better as whole, personally -- they get a <i>lot</i> of page count, especially compared to other splats antagonists, but there isn't much effort to make them interesting from a narrative perspective and I think that's a real shame. So much time and energy is put into making sure that the Beast's primary antagonist sucks, especially compared to the Beast, that I think it actually detracts from the game -- and that goes for mechanics too. Honestly, if you really wanna get your mileage out of Heroes, you're probably gonna need to homebrew a <i>lot</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:16:17-07:00","id":544629,"title":"","content":"I think the thing is that hero's greatest asset is forcing weaknesses on Beasts. Kind of a mechanical enforcement of why the hero rarely defeats the big boss monster of the story in the first encounter. With Beast the thing is that the Hero tends to be outclassed if we assume the Hero isn't in a different weight class than the Beast or getting extra assistance, but that first fight puts in some sort of breaker on the Beast that functions as an exceptionally annoying issue for the next fight. Like suddenly losing your powers because now you're weak to limestone or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:28:21-07:00","id":544634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544602#post544602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rater202, it <i>is</i> okay for people not to be as into the Hero vs Beast as-written-by-the-devs dynamic as you are, and you don't to jump into every protest about them feet first demanding that people see Heroes your way</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not at all what I did.<br /> <br /> See my post &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Regardless of personal opinions about heroes and the way they, the intent of the writers was that they are arrogant and self centered assholes with delusions of grandeur.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is literally all I said on the subject of <i>that</i> debate. Opinions aside, that is how the Writers intended them.<br /> <br /> That intent is important for this discussion, because that intent forms decisions about characterization and depiction of the heroes.<br /> <br /> A newbie hero being weaker than a newbie beast fits with the intent of heroes being self centered and delusional.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think this counts as a protest.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-07-2015, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:34:22-07:00","id":544635,"title":"","content":"In a straight-up fight, absolutely; if the Hero cheats, and they will, then they have a fairly good chance. The fact that you don't need a lot to be effective in combat as a Beast does kind of skew things in their favor, but with the right Gifts, especially Loremaster, Saint's Whisper, and the Weaponbound Anathema, a Beast can be pretty well screwed if they don't play pragmatically.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:47:46-07:00","id":544643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544634#post544634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not at all what I did.<br /> <br /> See my post &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Regardless of personal opinions about heroes and the way they, the intent of the writers was that they are arrogant and self centered assholes with delusions of grandeur.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is literally all I said on the subject of <i>that</i> debate. Opinions aside, that is how the Writers intended them.<br /> <br /> That intent is important for this discussion, because that intent forms decisions about characterization and depiction of the heroes.<br /> <br /> A newbie hero being weaker than a newbie beast fits with the intent of heroes being self centered and delusional.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think this counts as a protest.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>And I think that that should be the key to how you design the kinds of Heroes your troupe runs into. Their experience and level of tactical efficacy should be more or less directly proportional to the group's experience level, and inversely to the amount of desperation involved in the incident that created them and the regularity at which they are encountered. In other words: unless everyone's a month or two away from Incarnation, or have lately been eating well and actively avoiding the chance of a Hero showing up, most Heroes you build should be a bit chumpy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T19:10:58-07:00","id":544647,"title":"","content":"All I can say is &quot;Not the way I would play them.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't run a game of Hunter for a year without learning how the underdogs bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T19:11:59-07:00","id":544648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544643#post544643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I think that that should be the key to how you design the kinds of Heroes your troupe runs into. Their experience and level of tactical efficacy should be more or less directly proportional to the group's experience level, and inversely to the amount of desperation involved in the incident that created them and the regularity at which they are encountered. In other words: unless everyone's a month or two away from Incarnation, or have lately been eating well and actively avoiding the chance of a Hero showing up, most Heroes you build should be a bit chumpy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think we do have to agree that the situation you intend to evoke with a Hero has to factor into the level of difficulty. I mean if you want to have kind of a mid story &quot;this is how far you've come&quot; so you have them fight one Hero who's about on par with the first Hero boss they fought; then it will be expected that this Hero is going to be chump change. If the goal was to give them a fight to show how desperate their situation is, so they've fought one of the Guilds in Japan. Then I have to imagine lack of chump will be integral.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T20:34:32-07:00","id":544733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544647#post544647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can say is &quot;Not the way I would play them.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't run a game of Hunter for a year without learning how the underdogs bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Tucker's Kobolds is an object example that underdogs with proper tactics are <i>terrifying</i>. So that's nothing surprising.<br /> <br /> My issue is that Beasts can effectively &quot;outgrow&quot; Heroes being a threat in a way that other game lines don't. If I'm a Vampire, the Strix are <i>always</i> terrifying. Same with Werewolves and the Pure, or Mages and the Abyss, and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> Heroes just seem excessively out of their league, especially since Beasts are <i>really</i> dangerous, combat-wise; there are <i>at least</i> two Atavisms where the whole &quot;leaving Heroes alive is an issue&quot; thing <i>isn't</i> an issue, because the chance of them surviving a fight with you are slim to none.Beasts have enough numbers inflation that Heroes can't really keep up unless they have lots more XP, are backed by an army of people, or have a small armory at their beck and call. And at that point, <i>anything</i> is dangerous, so why even bother giving them special mechanics.<br /> <br /> I have no issue with Heroes being the underdog (it'd be weird if they weren't, really), but need a little more <i>inherent</i> punch. I'd be happy with a buff to Anathema, but I feel that the powers should have a <i>bit</i> more oomf.<br /> <br /> <b>SUMMARY</b><br /> Hearing that a Hero is on their trail should make the players sweat a little; right now, it's something that they could take in stride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:14:15-07:00","id":544751,"title":"","content":"The most viable &quot;end game&quot; requires making heroes a nuisance rather than a threat.<br /> <br /> For that to happen, the heroes have to be a threat that can be out grown.<br /> <br /> And being something that can be outgrown is consistent with the intent of the writers in the default hero depiction.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words &quot;hearing an <i>experienced </i>Hero is on their trail should make them sweat a little. Hearing a green Hero is on their trail should make the players feed or starve themselves, and double check their security to make sure the annoying little bugger can't catch them by surprise or slap one of those bullshit weaknesses on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:31:34-07:00","id":544765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544733#post544733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>SUMMARY</b><br /> Hearing that a Hero is on their trail should make the players sweat a little; right now, it's something that they could take in stride.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying you're wrong, but,well, Tucker's Kobolds.<br /> <br /> They can do with more, I grant you, but it's not like players depends on the tools to fear them. They depend on the storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:52:17-07:00","id":544787,"title":"","content":"Plus unless you are the one who created the Hero, you should find out a Hero is after by said Hero trying to 'thwart' one of your 'evil schemes'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T22:37:19-07:00","id":544820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544602#post544602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as OP -- I think Heroes honestly could have been written better as whole, personally -- they get a <i>lot</i> of page count, especially compared to other splats antagonists, but there isn't much effort to make them interesting from a narrative perspective and I think that's a real shame. So much time and energy is put into making sure that the Beast's primary antagonist sucks, especially compared to the Beast, that I think it actually detracts from the game -- and that goes for mechanics too. Honestly, if you really wanna get your mileage out of Heroes, you're probably gonna need to homebrew a <i>lot</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes are Beast's primary antagonists according to whom? Heroes? Heroes are delusional.<br /> <br /> The chances that a beast will go hungry for extended periods of time, considering getting satiety is trivially easy, in range of someone who just happens to be so emotionally balanced they're in slasher territory, and get a critical failure or success? That's not going to happen often.<br /> <br /> Mortals, including hunters, legal authorities, and outraged mobs ala hurt locker, fellow beasts, and other supernaturals are going to come up far more often than hunters.<br /> <br /> Heroes are a side effect, like disquiet stirred muggles in promethean, or abyssal spirits summoned by an unlucky paradox result","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T23:04:11-07:00","id":544845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544820#post544820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heroes are Beast's primary antagonists according to whom? Heroes? Heroes are delusional.<br /> <br /> The chances that a beast will go hungry for extended periods of time, considering getting satiety is trivially easy, in range of someone who just happens to be so emotionally balanced they're in slasher territory, and get a critical failure or success? That's not going to happen often.<br /> <br /> Mortals, including hunters, legal authorities, and outraged mobs ala hurt locker, fellow beasts, and other supernaturals are going to come up far more often than hunters.<br /> <br /> Heroes are a side effect, like disquiet stirred muggles in promethean, or abyssal spirits summoned by an unlucky paradox result</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the book, mostly. And, y'know, the developers, Heroes are the main antagonist for Beast. Are they necessarily the main antagonists you're going to use in Beast? No, because it's your game. Are they the main antagonists if you decide Beast is not going to be a crossover game (which you can do, actually, even if it's designed to be explicitly crossover friendly? Again, according to the book and the developers?) quite possibly, because they're literally the <i>only antagonists that get any description</i>. There are no factions of specifically antagonistic Beasts. There are no other antagonists clearly outlined in the book; Heroes are, by default, the main antagonist for Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T00:04:13-07:00","id":544868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544765#post544765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying you're wrong, but,well, Tucker's Kobolds.<br /> <br /> They can do with more, I grant you, but it's not like players depends on the tools to fear them. They depend on the storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tucker's Kobolds rely very very heavily on a home-field advantage designed specifically for their strengths. You're missing the fact that it's the BEAST, not the Hero, who has the home-field advantage. If we're going to use Tucker's Kobolds as an example, then that should only make Beasts even stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T00:12:31-07:00","id":544871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544868#post544868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tucker's Kobolds rely very very heavily on a home-field advantage designed specifically for their strengths. You're missing the fact that it's the BEAST, not the Hero, who has the home-field advantage. If we're going to use Tucker's Kobolds as an example, then that should only make Beasts even stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're forgetting the part where the kobolds were holed up where the adventurers wanted to go.<br /> <br /> Yes, Beast's carry their home turf with them, but anyone who's read of clever trickster heroes knows that there's more than one way to get a fox out of their burrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T01:17:15-07:00","id":544913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you#post544507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heroes are... rather underwhelming - am I the only one who gets this impression?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I missed something, but Beasts can be killed by murdering their human body, right? A hero doesn't necessarily need to enter and destroy the Lair's heart chamber?<br /> If that's the case, they are strong enough. Beasts get some very good defensive powers, but nothing that can't be met with the right tactics and surprise.<br /> Beasts with the anti-surprise powers are probably the biggest problem, but enough remote detonated explosives can fix that.<br /> Some others are immune to specific tactics, for example fire bombing them where they don have resonance with their lair won't work against the fire immune ones.<br /> But as a rule, most Beasts are the kind of problem you can fix with a sniper rifle, a truck going at high speed, or a surprise shotgun to the back of the head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T02:03:45-07:00","id":544922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544913#post544913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if I missed something, but Beasts can be killed by murdering their human body, right? A hero doesn't necessarily need to enter and destroy the Lair's heart chamber?<br /> If that's the case, they are strong enough. Beasts get some very good defensive powers, but nothing that can't be met with the right tactics and surprise.<br /> Beasts with the anti-surprise powers are probably the biggest problem, but enough remote detonated explosives can fix that.<br /> Some others are immune to specific tactics, for example fire bombing them where they don have resonance with their lair won't work against the fire immune ones.<br /> But as a rule, most Beasts are the kind of problem you can fix with a sniper rifle, a truck going at high speed, or a surprise shotgun to the back of the head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Beasts can be a fair bit more resilient than a normal person, so those might not work as well even if you're targeting the human and not the troll. I can't recall much specifics in the mechanics, but I think it is fair to say that slaying one of the Children can be done in the normal world and doesn't require entering the lair and slaying the Orochi to take one out. It is however fair to say that many a Hero will take the attempt on the grounds of it making them sound more impressive and fewer potential hazards of law enforcement or the like stepping in to stop the Hero from murdering the crap out of the Worm that Walk. I am pretty sure one of the fluff pieces mentioned a hero getting his first kill by catching his boss alone in the office and getting the killing on before she could really rally against him.<br /> <br /> Oh though I think killing the human form does occasionally risk the Beast's soul becoming one of the Unfettered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T02:47:59-07:00","id":544942,"title":"","content":"Heroes that Survive should Generally become Masters of the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IndyPloy\" target=\"_blank\">Indie Ploy</a> or Straight up <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Badass\" target=\"_blank\">Badasses.</a><br /> Add a Touch of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CrazyPrepared\" target=\"_blank\">Batman Preperation</a>... and Well. Beasts need to worry.<br /> <br /> Straight out the Gate it Should all depend, A Hero should be a Constant Threat even if not a Physical one until he/she learns a &quot;Weakness&quot; of the Beast and Then they will strike.. and Flee if need be.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just Thinking about it... Heroes should be... Well. Too use them Properly they Should be Ahabs. They WILL Get the monster Even if it takes Years (And i Still like the idea that in the NWoD you should NEVER give Humans Prep time... they will absolutely destroy you if you do.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-08-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T05:37:03-07:00","id":545087,"title":"","content":"You should see it from the narrative point of view (Wyrd?) rather than the mechanics. <br /> For example: no matter how OP may be Smaug, or the fact he is resting on his Lair, Thorin <i> will </i> manage to find a way to screw him and become King Under the Mountain . Smaug <i>will </i> die due to a very convenient flaw in his jewel armor that Bilbo, sent there as Thorin's proxy, will discover. The usually Genre Savvy Smaug will catch the Villain Ball and leave the dwarves and the treasure for some petty revenge against the villagers. <br /> Of course, Thorin <i>will</i> be so ingrateful, arrogant, greedy and plain crazy to concede it was a one time Hunter like Bard who actually shoot the Beast down , or that Lake Villagers deserve some monetary retribution for their past hospitality and having lost their homes by Thorin and co. damn Quest. Heroes are just like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 06-08-2015, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:25:04-07:00","id":545873,"title":"","content":"I love a good underdog story and after reading the types of Heroes that exist, I love the feel of the Tyrant's Hero, the lower class revolutionary going up against The Corporate Man that the Tyrant seems to personify. Of course they are filled with delusion of grandeur from their first meet with the Beast and may or may not have already fallen off the Moral Event Horizon, they'll likely be continually under the thumb and crapped on by their Beast, though I think the conflict as a whole makes a great story and a Beast may not want to end the life of the Hero when they beat them, because of a whole bunch of reasons due to personality and narrative.<br /> In that way, I like the possibilities of Beast and how it does a more narrative way of asking someone who they may be in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:35:14-07:00","id":545882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you#post544507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, comparing the rules for Beasts to those for Heroes suggests that Beasts will <i>annihilate</i> Heroes unless the Hero is <i>much</i> more experienced than the Beast, or you have a team of Heroes ganging up on a Beast.<br /> <br /> Heroes are... rather underwhelming - am I the only one who gets this impression?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't forget that Heroes have the power of Anathema, in which they can impose weaknesses to Beasts and make them vulnerable. Say for example, the Hero wants to slay a Dragon, and believes their sword is a holy blade which cleaves through dragon scales like parchment. Suddenly the ordinary sword can now pierce the Dragon's Atavisms and sears their flesh on contact. Heroes are just humans, true, but they have supernatural powers to make up for their weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-08-2015, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:57:51-07:00","id":545918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544942#post544942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes that Survive should Generally become Masters of the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IndyPloy\" target=\"_blank\">Indie Ploy</a> or Straight up <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Badass\" target=\"_blank\">Badasses.</a><br /> Add a Touch of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CrazyPrepared\" target=\"_blank\">Batman Preperation</a>... and Well. Beasts need to worry.<br /> <br /> Straight out the Gate it Should all depend, A Hero should be a Constant Threat even if not a Physical one until he/she learns a &quot;Weakness&quot; of the Beast and Then they will strike.. and Flee if need be.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just Thinking about it... Heroes should be... Well. Too use them Properly they Should be Ahabs. They WILL Get the monster Even if it takes Years (And i Still like the idea that in the NWoD you should NEVER give Humans Prep time... they will absolutely destroy you if you do.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Batman prep relies on the following.<br /> <br /> 1 - weeks or possibly even months of planning.<br /> <br /> 2 - military grade hardware and resources.<br /> <br /> 3 - Batman knowing what he's up against first.<br /> <br /> A lot of times Batman got his ass kicked in the first fight, and I don't think a Beast is going to spare a hero once they know they're after them. The Hero will probably be under the presumption that the Beast will chain them to a saw mill and leave the room. In reality, the Beast is going to hand feed the Hero into the wood chipper to make sure the job is done right!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:13:51-07:00","id":545941,"title":"","content":"Banes and having a Weaponbound Anathema placed on your Beast character is a very scary prospect. And because all it takes is a Willpower point and a successful attack roll after making the annoucement that the Hero is doing such an attack, that's pretty scary.<br /> <br /> Here's a question, can a Beast suffer from multiple Anathemas and can a single Hero place more than the one onto the Beast. Because the willpower doesn't come back until the Anathema gets dispelled or the Beast is killed, they're not going to crazy with them, but is it possible for a single Hero to place perhaps two different Anathemas on a Beast in an encounter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:31:16-07:00","id":546267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=545941#post545941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question, can a Beast suffer from multiple Anathemas and can a single Hero place more than the one onto the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly no, which is part of why I love the implications of Weaponbound so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:45:03-07:00","id":546277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=546267#post546267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explicitly no, which is part of why I love the implications of Weaponbound so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>This also makes Apex easier if it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:52:20-07:00","id":546289,"title":"","content":"Probably going off tangent here, but...<br /> <br /> As an avid Demon player, the Heroes remind me a lot of the Knights of Adrian, especially in terms of the mechanics and aesthetics. I also love how the Heroes and the Knights are polar opposites because while the Knights are practical in their intentions (hell, more practical than most of the other Hunter compacts and conspiracies) the Heroes are fanatical and ideological. Also that the Knights have their 'boss' in God Machine and its angels, while the Heroes (at least for the moment) do not.<br /> <br /> The Heroes also kind of remind me of oWod Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T22:58:12-07:00","id":546554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=544845#post544845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the book, mostly. And, y'know, the developers, Heroes are the main antagonist for Beast. Are they necessarily the main antagonists you're going to use in Beast? No, because it's your game. Are they the main antagonists if you decide Beast is not going to be a crossover game (which you can do, actually, even if it's designed to be explicitly crossover friendly? Again, according to the book and the developers?) quite possibly, because they're literally the <i>only antagonists that get any description</i>. There are no factions of specifically antagonistic Beasts. There are no other antagonists clearly outlined in the book; Heroes are, by default, the main antagonist for Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh really? Where, page number please, I missed it.<br /> <br /> What I didn't miss is that heroes can be fixed by increasing their integrity, which among other things would mean receiving psychological help, yes?<br /> <br /> So the main antagonists for dragons, sea monsters, gorgons, giants who make the earth tremble with each step, can be vanquished utterly by a psychiatrist. <br /> <br /> Also the fact that there are beasts who can cure heroes by just telling them to grow up. What kind of main antagonist is completely utterly irrelevant to some of their antagonists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:33:18-07:00","id":546581,"title":"","content":"I'd say if thematically appropriate also that a Hero can get Beats from having damage in their last health boxes, Conditions placed on them or choosing Dramatic Failures, same as PCs. This means that as they fight Beasts, they slowly build up the path to buy up Integrity on their own. Whether this comes from beating the need out on Beasts until they're done, having the fight beaten out of them, to them just making proactive choice to letting the Beast one-up them for whatever reason, they can work to gain their humanity back. Now buying a dot in Integrity takes 3 Experience, so that's 15 Beats altogether. Still a good couple of scrapes to throw at the Beast PCs and show a bit of character development for their antagonist(s) as the campaign builds to whatever the plot's natural conclusion is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:43:40-07:00","id":546591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=546554#post546554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the fact that there are beasts who can cure heroes by just telling them to grow up. What kind of main antagonist is completely utterly irrelevant to some of their antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an Apex Beast. The process for becoming an Apex already requires a rank 9 or 10 lair rating and then you have to utterly destroy a Hero to the point where the beast has to basically have been controlling the conflict the entire time and then destroy the Hero without taking damage or falling victim to an anathema. They also aren't stated to cure Hero's the book implies that they can just shut down a Hero's power. The point of them is that they're supposed to be an existence beyond the Pcs capable of doing things they can't. So that complaint is basically arguing issues with the intrigue of Vampire because the Antediluvians are all walking extinction events.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 06-09-2015, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:05:06-07:00","id":546611,"title":"","content":"*nods* It'd have to be a fairly ongoing campaign for a Beast to reach that point of becoming an Apex, unless starting with a high Starting Experience total at chargen or something, like an Urban Legend upwards. Then there are the issues to contend with in having a Lair that size also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:03:41-07:00","id":547958,"title":"","content":"So I'm trying to think how one would improve Heroes as far as making it feel like they can actually feel like they can be a threat to Beasts without potentially crossing the line of making them more dangerous than the Beast. Like if I'm not forgetting something a Beast can only suffer one anathema at a time, so even if they're fighting multiple Heroes only the most powerful anathema sticks. I get the logic of putting a low limit on anathema because, to use an extreme end, if Beasts had no limit to the number they could suffer under then you end up with nightmare scenarios where a group of Heroes goes in against the PCs and those that manage to survive come out with half a dozen weak spots, a weakness to every model of rifle at the local sporting store, and being horribly repulsed by almost every form of weather known to man that wouldn't directly contradict the Beast's nature.<br /> <br /> What I'm wondering is what would the middle point be? You know what's that happy medium where a well prepared Hero goes in decked to take advantage of every weakness the Beast has, but without giving the Beast so many weaknesses that these preparations unbalance the fight and make the Beast the underdog in the conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:53:34-07:00","id":547989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=547958#post547958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm trying to think how one would improve Heroes as far as making it feel like they can actually feel like they can be a threat to Beasts without potentially crossing the line of making them more dangerous than the Beast. Like if I'm not forgetting something a Beast can only suffer one anathema at a time, so even if they're fighting multiple Heroes only the most powerful anathema sticks. I get the logic of putting a low limit on anathema because, to use an extreme end, if Beasts had no limit to the number they could suffer under then you end up with nightmare scenarios where a group of Heroes goes in against the PCs and those that manage to survive come out with half a dozen weak spots, a weakness to every model of rifle at the local sporting store, and being horribly repulsed by almost every form of weather known to man that wouldn't directly contradict the Beast's nature.<br /> <br /> What I'm wondering is what would the middle point be? You know what's that happy medium where a well prepared Hero goes in decked to take advantage of every weakness the Beast has, but without giving the Beast so many weaknesses that these preparations unbalance the fight and make the Beast the underdog in the conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about one anathema per hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:15:15-07:00","id":553325,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that Anathema don't even work unless the Beast is at middle Satiety. Or rather, they can't be applied. It seems like it would be very easy to play a consistently low Satiety Beast. Sure, you spawn more Heroes, but Atavisms are more powerful at low Satiety and Anathema don't work, making a low Satiety Beast a completely unfair fight for most Heroes unless they're already suffering from a previously applied Anathema. It's child's play (1 atavism, 4 merit dots) to make a Beast with 6/3 armor at low Satiety, at that point a even shotgun to the chest isn't going to do much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:41:39-07:00","id":553340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=547989#post547989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about one anathema per hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there would still need to be some kind of cap on the number you can suffer at a given time. That a hero can't apply than more to a given beast is a good idea.<br /> <br /> @HelmsDerp Yeah honestly I'd like for there to be a high satiety way out of anathema as well. The anathema could probably benefit from either giving stronger heroes the power to potentially get an anathema to stick on Beasts out of the normal range or just having it, so those states don't offer blanket immunity so much as high resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:22:59-07:00","id":553409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=553340#post553340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@HelmsDerp Yeah honestly I'd like for there to be a high satiety way out of anathema as well. The anathema could probably benefit from either giving stronger heroes the power to potentially get an anathema to stick on Beasts out of the normal range or just having it, so those states don't offer blanket immunity so much as high resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div> Some of the conditions are from Slumber instead of Ravaging. They go both ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:10:26-07:00","id":553562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=553340#post553340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there would still need to be some kind of cap on the number you can suffer at a given time. That a hero can't apply than more to a given beast is a good idea.<br /> <br /> @HelmsDerp Yeah honestly I'd like for there to be a high satiety way out of anathema as well. The anathema could probably benefit from either giving stronger heroes the power to potentially get an anathema to stick on Beasts out of the normal range or just having it, so those states don't offer blanket immunity so much as high resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't forget that Heroes do not work well with others if they even try to do so at all. So 1 Anathema per Hero seems reasonable. You're not going to have an organized squadron of Heroes going after the same Beast unless you've got a bad ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T00:04:42-07:00","id":737173,"title":"","content":"Sorry for thread necromancy, but Heroes aren't supposed to stand toe to toe with reasonably powerful Beasts who have Atavisms and Lair Traits. Gifts and Anathemas are there to even the playing field somewhat, and you can homebrew special ones for Heroes who kill Beasts with Lair 6+. For example, a Gift from a Namtaru with Unbreakable which upgrades the Heroes Armor against Beasts from 2/0 to 3/2. Another Gift from an Eshmaki with Relentless Hunter grants immunity to the Stunned Tilt and lets the Hero spend 1 willpower point to roll Stamina + Resolve to heal lethal damage equal to successes or all bashing damage. A third Gift from an Anakim with Cyclopean Strengthvthat gives 8 Again to all of the Hero's Strength rolls. There could be a Gift that adds the Hero's Resolve to his Health. A Hero who defeats an Incarnate Beast might get truly epic Gifts. I also house rule that Heroes can have Advanced and Epic Merits, with some modifications for the lack of a Horror. All in all, the power level of Heroes should be roughly proportional to that of your Brood or lone Beast, with epic Gifts if nevessary. And never forget that there are no lines that they will not cross for just the chance to kill a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-29-2015, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T05:30:48-07:00","id":737795,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, If I may I want to share my impression of this whole discussion.<br /> Now, I'm still reading the manual, but for what I have checked about heroes in it and in other discussions, I think people are limiting themselves \u200bregarding on how to use heroes.<br /> You see, for me Beast is a game about turning around the pop culture idea of classical myths where the hero is a noble warrior who slays the evil monster, when in reality it's the story of a narcissistic asshole who is stalking and trying to kill a creature that, although it can be monstrous and evil, it's no less a person than he is. It is a game about two deeply troubled souls, one who has a consciousness but has to struggle with dark impulses, and the other a deluded and insecure person who's searching for meaning and recognition.<br /> More than the danger of the hero killing the beast, I believe that there is a lot of potential for roleplaying and drama.<br /> Why it has to end in combat? Why not play with the idea of rejecting the classical stories? Like some people have pointed out, why not try and heal the hero? Or how about if the hero is the one that saves the beast from itself?.<br /> Of course there can be combat and violence, but at least for me that's is not the main purpose of the game. The climax of the story is when both the beast and the hero have learned a lesson and gained wisdom as a result. It can end in dead yes, but no conflict is worth having without risks. Think about what kind of feelings and emotions the hero and the beast awake in each other, what they mean to each other, and how they each change as a result.<br /> I hope that my post helps you, have cool games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-29-2015, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T15:28:04-08:00","id":764442,"title":"","content":"Think we'll get a book DEVOTED to heroes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T15:36:36-08:00","id":764447,"title":"","content":"If not, they might get a section in a night horrors style book for beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:13:50-08:00","id":764668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544507-beast-do-heroes-seem-a-bit-anaemic-to-you?p=764447#post764447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If not, they might get a section in a night horrors style book for beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as, say, the upcoming <b>Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consum